PArc's own code (MIT): bwt_core.c — the runtime without the C library (memory functions, the
allocator hook, ___chkstk_ms for mingw), the LZP encoder (the algorithm of src/parc_lzp.pas,
same bytes), the repeat-share estimate and the segmentation sweep, and the entry points.

build.sh compiles bwt_core.c (which includes libsais.c and qlfc.c) for every target with
-O3 -fno-builtin -ffreestanding -fno-stack-protector (and -fno-tree-loop-distribute-patterns
with gcc); the object needs nothing from the C library or libgcc. To update libsais, replace
libsais.c/libsais.h and check that `nm -u` of the object is still empty on every target.
